{"name":"Beech","hex":"#5b4f3b","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Beech","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A village and civil parish west of Alton, East Hampshire district, Hampshire, England .","An unincorporated community in Warren County, Iowa, United States."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An aircraft made by Beechcraft."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Beech"}],"entries":[{"title":"Beech","blocks":[{"text":"Beech is a genus of deciduous trees in the family Fagaceae, native to subtropical and temperate Eurasia and North America. There are 14 accepted species in two distinct subgenera, Englerianae Denk & G.W.Grimm and Fagus. The subgenus Englerianae is found only in East Asia, distinctive for its low branches, often made up of several major trunks with yellowish bark. The better known species of subgenus Fagus are native to Europe, western and eastern Asia and eastern North America."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Beech-tree.JPG/330px-Beech-tree.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beech"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/367_Fagus_silvatica.jpg/120px-367_Fagus_silvatica.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/367_Fagus_silvatica.jpg/250px-367_Fagus_silvatica.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/367_Fagus_silvatica.jpg/120px-367_Fagus_silvatica.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A367_Fagus_silvatica.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Fagus_sylvatica_leaf_001.jpg/250px-Fagus_sylvatica_leaf_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org